metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-12 : List (List Word)
metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-12 = cons "## Metacircular: the system is one of its stateboxes" (cons "" (cons "John McCarthy's Lisp (1960) defined its own evaluator in Lisp. John Reynolds named the move metacircular in Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order Programming Languages (1972): a language defined by an interpreter written in the language it defines. Brian Cantwell Smith's 3-Lisp (1982) built the reflective tower, a program able to step up and reason about its own interpretation." (cons "" (cons "Hyperactivity is metacircular as a whole system: everything but the core C is written in the language itself: the command `hyperactive`, the guard on every commit, the views of the workflow, the server, decomposition, history and onboarding are hyperactive code, checked by the checker they run on. The paper's own opening is the same claim at the scale of the universe: the universe is not one of the objects outside which its description takes place; it includes the text, its author and its reader, and the observer and its reasoning are included in the evolution they describe. The workflow is a statebox in the store; the agents who walk the onboarding and do the work are participants in the unison; the knowledge graph that records the work is itself work recorded. Closure under reflection (§9.2) is the theorem form: the system's account of itself is one of its values." (cons "" (cons "Metacircularity closes the circle. Held by itself, every part of the system is subject to the same identity, the same transport and the same witnesses as everything it holds." (cons "" nil)))))))
